Created the package, holding what the Volto and Aurora frontends share: the REST payload types, the vocabulary names, a table of every REST path, the helpers that need no frontend framework, the login components, and the card shown when a provider sends the user back. The components take their translations, links, icons and the frontend's own page paths from an `IdentityUIProvider` that each frontend supplies, and fall back to English, plain links, plain icons and Volto's paths without one. Their styles are plain CSS, and the design tokens and base classes they read ship with the package in `styles.css`, so a frontend restyles them by redefining the `--identity-*` custom properties and needs no Sass compiler. @sneridagh
